<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain Rojo reappointed EMI vicepresident.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain Rojo reappointed EMI vicepresident.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain's governor Luis Angel Rojo has been reappointed vice-president of the European Monetary institute, the Spanish central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Rojo was first appointed the position in June 1994.</p>
<p>Two days ago Alexandre Lamfalussy was replaced as EMI president by Win Duisemberg bringing to an end Rojo's appointment.</p>
<p>But Duisemberg asked him to remain, a spokesman at the Bank of Spain said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
</text>
